  "244": {
    "action": "confirm",
    "canonical": "Terminate TCP/TLS at a Layer 7 reverse-proxy or edge front end as close to the user as possible \u2014 keeping long-lived, pre-warmed encrypted connections to backends \u2014 to minimise handshake round-trip latency and to absorb low-level attacks (e.g. SYN floods) and slow-client buffering that backend termination cannot handle."
  },
  "245": {
    "action": "confirm",
    "canonical": "Health-check backends and give each an explicit 'lame-duck' state in which it keeps serving in-flight requests but asks clients to stop sending new ones (propagated to active and, via periodic health checks, inactive clients), so backends can be drained, removed, or updated without disrupting user requests."
  },
